;; byj-gly.113 — the permission-gate set, built to lev's PRESET SHAPE after the
;; first set (lev_routing_set.edn) was shown to violate it six ways.
;;
;; What this set does differently, each tied to lev's README or workflows/triage.clj:
;;   - the state is short and structured, with named keys (`tool`, `command`,
;;     `cwd`) that the instructions reference in backticks, as every preset does;
;;   - four questions share one forward pass, not one question per call;
;;   - three nouls plus one 3-option choice, which is triage's mix, rather than a
;;     single 10-way choice (the shape lev's own bench is weakest at);
;;   - the options are one or two words, so the 192-token head budget is not
;;     eaten and the option texts are not silently shrunk.
;;
;; LABELS. :destructive and :scope are close to objective — whether a command
;; deletes or overwrites data, and how far its effect reaches, are properties of
;; the command. :reversible and :needs-approval carry judgement, and the entries
;; where reasonable people would differ are marked :borderline true so the
;; analysis can report accuracy with and without them. Nothing here is harvested:
;; this repo ships no deny-list (`:bash-deny-commands` defaults to []) and its
;; trajectories contain no bash commands, so the commands are authored — which is
;; exactly why the LLM baseline is run again as a check on the labels.
